{"santizeAnchors implementation is brittle - iterates over anchors and mutates translated value in a way that can misreport or drop anchors if they occur in different order or there are multiple anchors": 0.7372512817382812, "Build-time vs. runtime sanitization enforcement contradiction - finding claims sanitization is only enforced at build time while another finding shows sanitizer is wired into Freemarker rendering at request time, requiring investigation to determine actual enforcement boundary": 0.13397911190986633, "HTML unescaping is applied after sanitization (via StringEscapeUtils.unescapeHtml4 or fixURLs) without re-running the sanitizer, which can reverse the sanitizer's escaping and reintroduce unsafe HTML tags or attributes into the final output": 0.2710656523704529, "Regex in normalizeValue for templateHelp does not account for space before closing angle bracket in CLAIM placeholders (e.g., 'CLAIM.<NAME >'), so placeholders may not be removed, potentially triggering false positives for HTML content in translations": 0.7828245162963867, "HREF_PATTERN regex only matches href attributes with double quotes, ignoring single-quoted href values which may allow some legitimate anchor URLs to bypass the post-sanitization URL unescaping logic (fixURLs)": 0.11534047871828079}